== txt2 ==
[[[markup]]] [++every keyword in English too++] [??never fails??]

txt2 is the markup of __XGM__ (https://xgm.guru), the Warcraft III modding site: its articles, resource pages and comments are written in it.
This file describes it and is written in it, so it shows every construct it describes. // README.md says the same in Markdown. //

((cut Contents
- Inline: emphasis, accents, labels, links, mentions, icons
- Blocks:
 1. headings, rules, quotes, spoilers, alignment, layouts
 2. code, lists, tables, progress bars
 3. images, videos, polls, tiles
- Errors
))

A text is lines. A line break is kept: these two lines
are two lines on the page, not one paragraph. Blank lines separate blocks.
What isn't markup is text, and a marker without its closing one stays as it is written: **open.

The site's keywords are Russian. Each has an English twin, and both are read the same:

Russian | English
---
{{((кат}} | {{((cut}}, {{((spoiler}}
{{((цитата}} | {{((quote}}
{{((центр}}, {{((вправо}} | {{((center}}, {{((right}}
{{((макет}}, {{((блок33}}, {{((блок50}}, {{((блок66}} | {{((layout}}, {{((block33}}, {{((block50}}, {{((block66}}
{{((код}} | {{((code}}
{{((опрос}}, {{мультивыбор}}, {{закрывается}} | {{((poll}}, {{multichoice}}, {{closes}}
{{((плитка}} | {{((tile}}
{{/иконка/}} | {{/icon/}}
{{в:}}, {{я:}} | {{wr:}}, {{y:}}

---

== Inline ==

markup | result
---
{{*word*}}, {{**several words**}} | *bold*, **several words**
{{_word_}}, {{__several words__}} | _italic_, __several words__
{{-word-}}, {{--several words--}} | -struck-, --several words--
{{!word!}}, {{!!several words!!}} | !accent!, !!accent 1, red!!
{{+word+}}, {{++several words++}} | +accent+, ++accent 2, green++
{{?word?}}, {{??several words??}} | ?accent?, ??accent 3, blue??
{{// aside //}} | text // aside // text
{{[[[label]]]}}, {{[!!…!!]}}, {{[++…++]}}, {{[??…??]}} | [[[label]]] [!!red!!] [++green++] [??blue??]
the text between two opening and two closing braces | {{*as it is*}}

A single marker wraps one word: it opens after something that isn't a letter or digit, and closes before one, with no space inside. So C++, snake_case, xgm-team, a - b and 5 * 3 stay text.
A double marker may wrap several words; a space may come before its closing one: !!Note: !!
Markers nest: **bold __and italic__**.

=== Links ===

markup | result
---
{{https://xgm.guru/p/xgm}} | https://xgm.guru/p/xgm
{{__several words__ (https://xgm.guru)}} | __several words__ (https://xgm.guru)
{{_word_ (https://xgm.guru)}} | _word_ (https://xgm.guru)
{{Word (https://xgm.guru)}} | Word (https://xgm.guru)
{{[Markdown style](https://xgm.guru)}} | [Markdown style](https://xgm.guru)
{{@XGM+Bot}}, {{~~XGM Bot~~}}, {{@p/xgm}} | @XGM+Bot, ~~XGM Bot~~, @p/xgm
{{w:Warcraft_III}}, {{wr:Warcraft_III}} | w:Warcraft_III, wr:Warcraft_III
{{g:txt2}}, {{y:txt2}}, {{s:txt2}} | g:txt2, y:txt2, s:txt2
{{/icon/flask}}, {{/icon/cube/2x}} | /icon/flask /icon/cube/2x

The schemes are http, https and ftp after {{://}}, and mailto, callto, skype, sip, sips, tg, steam, tel, bitcoin and facetime after {{:}}.
A bare link ends at a space: punctuation after it, or a closing parenthesis it didn't open, is not part of it.
A user's name has {{+}} for a space. Searches go to the English and the Russian Wikipedia, Google, Yandex and the site.
Icons are FontAwesome 6, 1x to 5x.

== Blocks ==

A block starts a line; spaces before it are allowed. Blocks that open run to their closing line, which is alone on its line, and blocks inside them are read as anywhere else.

=== Headings and rules ===

```
# Level 1 as in Markdown
## Level 2
== Level 2, as many = as the level ==
===Level 3
---
```

A line of one or more {{-}} is a rule:

---

