=== Code ===

```cpp
// Code keeps its lines as they are, with no *markup*.
class MyException: public Exception {}
```

""
Two quotes open and close code too.
""

((code jass
function Hello takes nothing returns nothing
    call BJDebugMsg("((code with a language")
endfunction
))

{{
{{ alone on its line opens text as it is, its lines kept: *no* !markup!.
}}

A fence closes at a line that is exactly the fence; with a space after it, the line is code.
The site highlights perl, php, css, xml, html, javascript, java, cpp, sql, jass, lua, delphi and dos.

=== Lists ===

- {{-}} and {{*}} start an item
* both are the same
 1. numbered items: digits and a dot
 2) or a parenthesis
  2.1. and dots between levels
- lines indented more than the marker belong to the item above

All items of a list share an indent; a blank line ends it.

=== Tables ===

A table starts after a blank line with a line holding {{|}}. Tabs work too, as pasted from a spreadsheet.

<> Header over two | < | >>> Right
---
two cells joined by {{<}} | < | one
two rows joined by {{^}} | a | b
^ | c {{|}} d | >>> right-aligned
four cells: {{<}} and {{^}} | < | e
^ | ^ | f

A line of {{-}} after the first rows makes them the header; the header joins only across. {{>>> text}} is right-aligned, {{<> text}} centered, and a {{|}} between two braces on each side is a {{|}} inside a cell, as in c {{|}} d.
Rows may have different numbers of cells.

=== Progress bars ===

[ 75% ] a share
[ 3 / 4 ] a count of a total
[ 4 / 3 - 19 ] a value between a minimum and a maximum
[ 01.01.2026 / 01.01.2027 ] a countdown between two dates, Moscow time

=== Images, videos, sounds ===

A link alone on its line embeds it: an image (png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, avif, bmp, svg), a video (YouTube, VK, Rutube, PLVideo, Twitch, Vimeo, Dailymotion, Bilibili, mp4, webm, ogg), a sound (mp3), or a GitHub gist.

https://xgm.guru/files/100/235701/minimap.png - the minimap's icons, with a caption

-> https://xgm.guru/files/100/235701/minimap.png - on the right
{{<-}}, {{->}} and {{<>}} before an image put it on the left, on the right or in the center of the text.
A caption follows {{ - }}, and {{(url)}} after an image makes it a link there.

https://xgm.guru/files/100/235701/minimap.png (https://xgm.guru)
https://xgm.guru/files/100/235701/minimap.png - two images, one line after the other: a gallery

=== Polls ===

((poll Which keywords do you write?
multichoice 1
closes 31.12.2030
Russian
English
Both
))

A poll has 2 to 32 options. {{multichoice N}} lets a voter choose N, half of them without a number; {{closes dd.mm.yyyy}} ends it at noon, Moscow time.

